package Libraries.Language.Compile.Test

use Libraries.Testing.QuorumTest
use Libraries.Testing.ScriptCheck

/*
ComputeTester runs the matrix multiply scripts in Scripts/Compute/Pass,
brought over from the compute shader project's CpuMultiplyTest and
HardwareMultiplyFallbackTest. Only the checks that a CPU can answer are
here; the tests that need a graphics card are not.

Back ends:
CpuMultiply uses Multiply:Transform and TransformInSoftware, plain CPU
code, so it runs on bytecode, JavaScript and Python. Multiply creates
shader code only for the graphics card, and its comment notes that Python
has no graphics card support, so the CPU path is meant to work everywhere.

MultiplyFallback calls TransformInHardware, which asks GameStateManager
for a compute device. On bytecode that looks for Vulkan, and the range
check sends these numbers to the CPU whether or not a card is found. In a
web browser GetComputeDevice finds no device, so JavaScript uses the CPU
too. Python can't look for a Vulkan device, so it is not run there.
*/
class ComputeTester
    QuorumTest suite = undefined
    ScriptCheck scripts
    text path = "Scripts/Compute/Pass/"

    action Test
        scripts:SetSuite(suite)
        scripts:Check(path + "CpuMultiply", true, true)
        scripts:Check(path + "MultiplyFallback", true, false)
    end

    action GetName returns text
        return "Compute Tests"
    end

    action GetCompilerTestSuite returns QuorumTest
        return suite
    end

    action SetCompilerTestSuite(QuorumTest suite)
        me:suite = suite
    end
end
